66	        { id: 'fields', eyebrow: `FIELDS · ${focusIndex || '—'} · FROM THE INDEX MAPPING`, cols: 6, type: 'fields',
67	          render: () => renderFields(fields),
68	        },
69	
70	        { id: 'howTo', eyebrow: 'WHERE THESE NUMBERS COME FROM', cols: 12, type: 'markdown',
71	          render: () => Markdown(
72	`## One connection, read live
73	
74	This node has one data source — its built-in engine — listed by
75	\`GET /_xerj-console/api/v1/data-sources/connections\`. Indices and fields
76	come from the same facade. Doc counts and store bytes are the engine's own
77	(\`Index::stats\` and the index's data directory), not estimates.
78	
79	The default connection is stored in \`localStorage.xerj.cluster\`, visible
80	under SETTINGS. The knowledge surface — sizes, per-dataset fields,
